Implement a real transaction parser.

Retrieve transaction data using getTransaction with a suitable encoding and maxSupportedTransactionVersion configuration.

Extract and normalize:

- Transaction signature.
- Slot.
- Block time, when available.
- Transaction version.
- Commitment or finality context.
- Execution success or failure.
- Error details.
- Transaction fee in lamports and SOL.
- Recent blockhash.
- Static account keys.
- Loaded writable addresses.
- Loaded read-only addresses.
- Required signatures.
- Signer accounts.
- Outer instructions.
- Inner instructions.
- Program invocation logs.
- Compute units consumed.
- Return data, when present.
- Pre-transaction SOL balances.
- Post-transaction SOL balances.
- Pre-token balances.
- Post-token balances.
- Token mint addresses.
- Token-account owners reported in metadata.
- Token decimals and raw token amounts.
- Address Lookup Table references.
- Compute Budget instructions.
- Account creation and closure instructions.
- Relevant program-specific instructions.

